  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "This paper studies QAOA on IBM bipotent superconducting QPUs, comparing direct-CX and ECR-CX gate implementations for 3-, 4-, and 5-qubit portfolio optimization and 5-qubit MaxCut instances. It reports that pulse-level optimized ECR-based gates, especially ZZ-SWAPOPT, can improve approximation ratio and success probability; for example, 5Q PortOpt reaches AR up to 0.909 in noiseless simulation and the 5Q MaxCut baseline reaches AR up to 0.997, but the paper does not demonstrate classical quantum advantage.",
